  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_cc34ffaf158448f88ba584241af393e2",
      "statement": "TransitCatalogService owns two in-process ManagedCatalog instances — bus (BusStopPoint, loaded via the fixed 45 km citywide selectNearStops.do query) and subway (SubwayStationPoint, loaded from the official T-Data CSV) — and serves /api/stops/nearby and /api/subway/nearby by filtering the full cached catalog with haversine geometry locally, while the arrivals endpoints (/api/arrivals/:arsId and /api/subway/arrivals) hit their live upstream on every request and are never catalog-cached.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/api/src/transit/transit.controller.ts#L32-L120",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:52eb6a43b5ce5e09ef8e18a0250623a22417ea90257329d433322c988c7ea477:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/api/src/transit/transitCatalog.service.ts#L33-L132",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e1f647d0b5f63fd9b93fc62fb89cc603435040cabd83b7254838f308551b47d0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1f7a11b8e0494e66b0e9187d58589d43",
      "statement": "ManagedCatalog refresh is single-flight: the private refresh() memoizes one in-flight loader promise (cleared in finally so the next refresh can start), so concurrent cold readers, scheduled timers, and stale reads share a single upstream call; the unit test pins two concurrent read() calls to one loader invocation and the e2e suite pins concurrent cold subway requests sharing one pending catalog load.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/api/src/transit/managedCatalog.test.ts#L27-L44",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ab11aeb675bb67a40f9e1b1331e4cdd2d7db5e3151e1101d40addaf4bdc699f6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/api/src/transit/managedCatalog.ts#L112-L117",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2c2820300222cd2f397970cd19f65e903f9daf87053ac89cd4346373ed92cd99:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/api/test/app.e2e.test.ts#L430-L474",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e17ea9f8bbbc37cee32d9de6892199a28a31071bf4ace1a3592cda485ece5f1e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_95464066db1446e0b66cbe7d30ce615b",
      "statement": "read() with no snapshot rethrows the stored lastError immediately and makes no upstream call while now() is before retryAfter (bounded cold-path backoff: one error per retryMs window instead of one per request); otherwise it awaits a cold-request refresh and returns that snapshot's items.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/api/src/transit/managedCatalog.ts#L66-L71",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b010712be7b80f79891cfd7d3644cb955ad251667dfb48e823582ac7fb6d4b28:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d5c26f9cd7a145da8c5ee5a8f7612500",
      "statement": "read() with an existing snapshot never blocks: it returns the current items regardless of age, and only kicks off a background stale-request refresh (whose rejection is swallowed) when all three conditions hold — snapshot age at or past refreshMs, no load in flight, and now() at or past retryAfter.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/api/src/transit/managedCatalog.ts#L73-L82",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:56a370592639dbb909faf1f0409432dddafd03bac91d626efff2391abaafd5f0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8965daca13884117a48bc445c2765a5d",
      "statement": "Snapshots are immutable and swapped atomically: a successful load assigns a fresh items-plus-updatedAt object and clears retryAfter and lastError, while a failed load leaves the previous snapshot untouched, so readers keep being served the stale-but-complete catalog indefinitely while refreshes keep failing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/api/src/transit/managedCatalog.test.ts#L46-L74",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3759f8387243dcb78f6fd168c502e11a584df651b299b368119a7fc4417f0ad3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/api/src/transit/managedCatalog.ts#L119-L160",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:448b9fae930cb8a3a46685ee02af9c0b4aef230b83554d3d89a9978f1726e84b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fdb05317076c44deb8834e06eae15d91",
      "statement": "ManagedCatalog.load() applies a minimum-count gate: a loader result whose items.length is below minimumItems throws UpstreamError (\"<source> catalog rejected\" with the contained count), so a truncated payload never becomes the cached catalog; the gate defaults to 1/1 (bus/subway) in AppModule.register for tests while production main.ts passes 10,000 bus and 100 subway.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/api/src/app.module.ts#L84-L85",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ddbf59f13e41b1c4f09fbf080cd9c6a771bd19de1cfddb16748eebfb8b94cbc8:"
        },
        {
