    {
      "id": "claim_01e9a757dbde4e008d332a1cec5f2ed2",
      "statement": "start() is a no-op unless options.schedule (the warmup knob) is enabled, in which case it fires an immediate warmup refresh with its error swallowed; stop() clears any pending timer and nulls nextRefreshAt without aborting an in-flight load; TransitCatalogService wires these to onModuleInit/onModuleDestroy, so with the default warmup=false the catalogs stay lazy and timer-free until the first cold request.",
      "evidence": [
