      "id": "claim_44727dd4d5f94a058fe0cb1924463f87",
      "statement": "Row-level and wholesale failure handling are deliberately complementary: the @mota/contracts normalizers drop isolated malformed rows (normalizeStopCatalog per-row safeParse; normalizeOfficialSubwayStationCatalog skipping bad CSV lines) so one bad row never discards thousands of good entries, while the minimum-count gate and adapter byte caps reject wholesale truncation or bloat as UpstreamError.",
