      "id": "claim_05c671af7c3d4c5bbb458732c21832f4",
      "statement": "GET /api/health reports each catalog's status non-gating: it always returns 200 status ok with transitCatalogs: bus and subway CatalogStatus (ready = a snapshot exists, count, updatedAt, lastErrorAt, nextRefreshAt as null-safe ISO strings), so an unloaded or backoff-stuck catalog shows ready false rather than failing the Compose healthcheck that probes this endpoint; the e2e suite pins the ready and count transition after the first nearby request.",
